{
  "audio": "005.without-a-harness.mp3",
  "paragraph": 5,
  "text": "Without a harness, talking to a language model API is completely stateless and blind. You send one prompt, receive one completion, and the interaction ends right there. Wrap that exact same API inside a harness, and everything changes. Now the model becomes an iterative controller connected to a live environment. It proposes an action, the harness runs it against real files or terminals, feeds the actual output back in, and lets the model adapt step by step until the job is done.",
  "transcript": "Without a harness, talking to a language model API is completely stateless and blind. You send one prompt, receive one completion, and the interaction ends right there. Wrap that exact same API inside a harness, and everything changes. Now the model becomes an iterative controller connected to a live environment. It proposes an action, the harness runs it against real files or terminals, feeds the actual output back in, and lets the model adapt step-by-step until the job is done.",
